2.4. Printing the Object

Before the printing step, once the slicing is complete, the printer needs to be set up. This involves loading the material into the printer and calibrating the printer. The printer needs to be leveled and the print bed needs to be adjusted to the correct height. After the printer is set up, the printing process can begin [21, 23]. The printer will start by heating the material and then extruding it through a nozzle. The nozzle moves back and forth, laying down the material layer by layer until the object is complete as shown in Figure 4 for metal printing and the same is true for other types of printing.

