3.4. Direct Metal Laser Sintering (DMLS)

Direct metal laser sintering (DMLS) is a 3D printing technology that has revolutionized the aerospace industry by enabling the production of high-performance metal parts with complex geometries as shown in Figure 8. DMLS is particularly useful for manufacturing aircraft components that require high strength, durability, and resistance to extreme temperatures and pressures [2, 6, 7, 10, 46]. Some of the aircraft components that are commonly manufactured using DMLS include turbine blades, engine components, heat exchangers, and brackets. DMLS is also used for prototyping and testing aerospace parts, allowing engineers to quickly iterate and refine their designs before moving to production. Overall, DMLS is a valuable tool for the aerospace industry, enabling the production of high-quality, lightweight components that are critical for the safe and efficient operation of the aircraft [5, 19].

